<http://data.silknow.org/object/8c14c940-3cb7-3c48-8250-04cd0586a840/observation/2>
        a                   crmsci:S4_Observation ;
        ecrm:P2_has_type    <http://data.silknow.org/observation/general-observation> ;
        ecrm:P3_has_note    "Bellows with the Arms of the Giustiniani and Rossi Families\nAbout 1530\n\nBellows, usually operated by servants, were a key piece of fireplace equipment. This pair bears the arms of two prominent Venetian families. The fantastical decoration, ranging from dolphins and mermaids to a puffing figure blowing into the pipe, suited the ornate setting of the camera d’oro. [44 words]\n\nItaly\nWalnut, partly gilded, with bronze, leather and silk velvet\n\nV&A: 7698-1861\nAt Home in Renaissance Italy, eds.Marta Ajmar-Wollheim and Flora Dennis (London, 2006), cat.125, pl.10.5 [5 Oct 2006 - 7 Jan 2007]"@en ;
        crmsci:O8_observed  <http://data.silknow.org/object/8c14c940-3cb7-3c48-8250-04cd0586a840> .

